  "id": "pfs",
  "term": "PFS",
  "definition": "PFS refers to posterior fossa syndrome, also called cerebellar mutism syndrome, a postoperative condition that can occur after removal of a posterior fossa brain tumour, mainly in children. It involves delayed reduced speech or mutism with emotional instability, often alongside motor, cognitive, behavioural, and other neurological changes.",
